PlatformOperatorRequired.description:
The caller is not an admitted platform operator. One code for every reason (no role, wrong
client, not on the allowlist, a bot) so the response does not reveal which check failed;
the reason is in the worker log and, when the token carried the role, the platform audit log.

ServeOverride.description:
A human decision that outranks the policy gate for one artefact. `block` always wins,
including over a passing policy; `allow` skips the policy check but never a manual block;
`null` clears the override and restores policy control.

PlatformFleetStuckArm.description:
One reaper arm. `build_*` and `scan_*` are provider_build_jobs / provider_scan_jobs;
`marker_*` are the shared provider_version_scans markers that hold the global in-flight
index; `module_version`, `state_version` and `plan_version` are the version scan reaper.

get.description:
The job row, its per-version/platform `provider_scan_results` rows (capped at 500;
`results_truncated` says more exist), and its flow, fetched from Argo as for builds.
`sbom_size: null` means no SBOM size was recorded, not a zero-byte SBOM.

value.rego:
package terramantle.policy

deny[msg] {
  input.findings[_].rule_id == "AVD-AWS-0107"
  msg := "security group open to the internet"
}

policies.rego:
